From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:19:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: don't re-upload push uniforms for a push that
 changes no bytes

vkCmdPushConstants flagged VS/FS (or compute) PUSH_UNIFORMS dirty on every
call, so the next draw re-packed the stage's FAUs into a new push-uniform
buffer and rewrote its FAU register. DXVK pushes the same constants again
after most pipeline changes: in Arkham Asylum (DXVK 1.10.3, D3D9) 10,039 of
10,182 pushes per second wrote the bytes already stored.

The upload is rebuilt from the push-constant storage and the sysvals, and
the sysvals have their own dirty tracking. If a push leaves the storage
unchanged, a stage whose dirty bit is clear and whose last upload was made
from the current storage would get identical push uniforms, so its bit can
stay clear. The storage is shared by all stages: a push that changes bytes
for some stages leaves the others' uploads made from the old bytes, so they
are recorded in stale_stages and an identical push still flags them. All
stages start stale at vkBeginCommandBuffer, after vkCmdExecuteCommands
(secondaries pointed the FAU registers at their own uploads; the compute
dirty state isn't reset there) and after meta operations.

PANVK_NO_PC_SAME_SKIP=1 flags the stages on every push again.

