Purpose: CPU: a vkCmdPushConstants that changes no bytes no longer re-uploads push uniforms for stages whose last upload used the current bytes (Arkham: 10,039 of 10,182 pushes/s identical); PANVK_NO_PC_SAME_SKIP=1 disables
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: rg477m/039 (stacked)
Validation test: drawcpu arkham mix with rg477m/041 667.4 -> 646.9 ns/draw (-3.1%), dxvk pattern -5.1%; DC_CHECKSUM colour identical on/off/base (arkham b590c25518c74c87, dxvk e5f8d186277b62c2); PanProbe 38/38 x2; combined build d6.so (443dfbaf1028, rg477m/023-041): 16-game boot sweep 2026-10-25 in quietd Stock mode (boot check, FPS limiter on): all 16 boot to their known states (Hades, Arkham, Serious Sam, Jupiter Hell, Risk of Rain 2, Moonlighter, Megabonk, Portal 2, Gladius, Crysis 3 Remastered render; Factorio and Ashes menus; Descenders; Tomb Raider ToS screen; Doom 3 BFG white window; Metro 2033 black), 0 GPU faults; uncapped gameplay A-B-B-A vs compat (quietd Stock, FPS limiter off): Hades hub at 1255 MHz 224.7 vs 224.9 fps (n=4 each, GPU-bound), Jupiter Hell tutorial level 48.5 vs 48.6 fps (n=4 each), Serious Sam bot benchmark D3D11 57.0 vs 58.9 fps (n=2 each), Risk of Rain 2 stage 1 27.6 vs 28.8 fps (n=5 each, random maps; the B17 memory guard ended 1 of 6 runs in each arm); Arkham Asylum 20-round interleaved gameplay gate 2026-10-25/26 (quietd Stock, FPS limiter off), base rg477m/023-037 vs this: gameplay fps 36.24 vs 36.25 (n=17 each), load failures (B5 signatures: appUncompressMemory/BulkData assertions, pure-virtual dialog) 2/19 vs 3/20 (B5 base rate: stock 7/38, ours 16/138), 0 GPU faults
